last year I recommended iPhone users to  buy the galaxy buds even though there  are certain limitations but a year later  things have changed both for Samsung and  for iOS so today I'll be answering if  the new galaxy buds plus are worth it  for iPhone users and if so what kind of  things do you gain and also miss out on  to get it right out there yes even  though we have the earpods Pro I think  for a lot of iOS users the galaxy buds  might actually be a better buy than air  pods but not for everybody and I'll tell  you exactly why in just a bit last year  I used the Galaxy buds with the nest 10  for about a week before trying it with  my iPhone but this time I skipped  Android altogether and went for a pure  iPhone experience which was made much  easier thanks to Samsung releasing an  iOS app just before launching the buds  plus let's start out with the first  enticement of the buds Plus and that's  the price they officially come in at $50  less than the second gen air pods with  wireless charging but if you buy through  our amazon link in the video description  the difference is only 20 bucks and if  you don't care about wireless charging  the air pots can be had for $10 cheaper  but in a lot of ways the galaxy butts  plus compete more so against the air  pods of pro which I've been happily  using ever since they came out and here  we have a $100 price difference the  second reason you might want to go with  the Galaxy buds plus is the battery life  the originals lasted about an hour more  than the air pods but the plus take it  to a whole nother level being rated at  more than doubled the battery life  thanks to better efficiency and a larger  battery now first I was skeptical about  this reading especially when changing  the EQ but in the real world they do  seem to get very close to that 11th hour  rating now I think most people don't  listen to their music for that long  without taking a break but if you're  somebody that listens for more than five  hours at a time the Galaxy buds will not  limit you at least in terms of battery  now comfort is a different story  personally I find the Galaxy buds to be  less comfortable than either ear pods  but I have heard the opposite from some  people now one thing that I am certain  of is that if you're a very active  person the adjustable wing tips included  give you a very good seal and even  though I don't have  issues with the air pods if you're  somebody that does I think the galaxy  buds will fit better another benefit is  that they don't stick out of your ears  looking like a toothbrush head or a mini  blow dryers so they work better with  hats or helmets if you're using them  like that you might want to use the  ambient mode last year this wasn't  available for iOS but now it is this is  great since the Galaxy buds used a seal  design but unfortunately even though the  ambient mode has gotten better it's  still far behind the pros and with the  air pods unseal design you don't need a  most like that now one thing that  surprised me was how quickly and  consistently they connected last year  they were okay but noticeably worse than  the air pods with the h1 chip but this  year my idea say that sometimes it seems  like they actually pair faster you do  miss out on iCloud integration so you  have to go into the settings of each iOS  or Mac device but the buds plus do  support multiple saved connections and  it will automatically disconnect from my  phone if I select them from my max  Bluetooth menu just like the air pods  now another reason to want the galaxy  buds plus for your iPhone is sound  quality even though they are quieter  than the air pods the buds absolutely  smoke the air pause and actually be out  the air pod pros as well once you tweak  the EQ out of the box they default to  the normal setting but changing that to  dynamic increases the output and bumps  up the mids and the highs while just  slightly decreasing the bass now sound  preferences are definitely subjective  but what isn't are the dual drivers at  the buds plus pack having two speakers  instead of one helps to keep the mids  and highs sounding rich and crisp while  maintaining good quality bass so if you  care about sound quality the galaxy buds  plus sound better and for $100 less one  feature you'll miss out on is the valve  that releases the pressure you get when  using sealed earbuds making them more  comfortable but on the plus side since  they don't have this they seal in most  of the audio whereas the air pods pros  have noticing a more sound leak in the  original ear pods well everybody could  just hear what you're listening to being  that be a seal in here you're  automatically going to block out noise  which air pods will do in our office  this gets rid of the louder than average  HVAC almost as good  as the airport pros active noise  cancellation but for louder noises like  airplanes the air pods do way better one  thing we didn't have to dive in too much  last year was software but now we have  the galaxy Budds app and new software  features through the air pods as well  now I'm glad the iOS users can now use  the AMD mo they could tweak their EQ  they could see their battery settings  for the case in the buds accurately and  you can customize what happens when you  use the controls including having  physical controls for volume which you  can't get with air pods but  unfortunately with an iPhone you're  still gonna miss out on a few features  compared to Android the first is the  gaming mode which lowers latency and  almost matches air pots on iOS since the  Galaxy buds also use AAC there's no lag  when watching videos but when playing a  game sounds will be more than half a  second off compared to just about a  hundred and fifty milliseconds so if you  play a lot of games on your iPhone  that's one area where the buds aren't  worth it the other feature you miss out  on is auto launching Spotify by tapping  on your bun but since you can use Siri  by pressing and holding in the touchpad  after the initial setup you could just  ask Siri to start playing music using  Spotify and that works almost as well in  fact she actually listened right now  when hos recording and turned on Spotify  the one feature you won't get with the  Galaxy buds Plus that I really enjoy is  hands-free Siri which works really well  to change volume launch apps play music  and one specific feature that we didn't  have a year ago which is see reading out  your text messages and allow you to  reply hands-free after I got used to  using hey Siri hands-free and this new  texting feature  I definitely miss it with the galaxy  buds overall if you don't need  hands-free Siri or very low latency in  games I think that the galaxy butts plus  absolutely destroy the original ear pods  especially if you want a sealed fit  I think they compare closer to the pros  than the originals even though they cost  $100 less and you get better sound  quality and battery life you do still  take a trade-off in terms of microphone  quality as you can hear for yourself  right here this are micron quality  during a call with the galaxy's buds  Plus this is a microphone quality during  a call with at the airport  if those Airport features don't matter  to you then the galaxy buds plus are  definitely worth it for iPhone users we  have links to the best deals down in the  video description and go ahead and let  me know what you think down in the  comment section below if you want to see  my full detailed review of the galaxy  buds plus click up there to subscribe  and if you want to see some more great  galaxy buds content we have some right  over there that's Ben Max and I will see  you in the next video  [Music]
 

